  "questions_for_authority": [
    "A raw.holding_history pair (original_trade_number, current_trade_number) whose only reports are all cdc_flag D currently produces no logical.holding_change row at all: with no I, U, or historical (null cdc_flag) candidate, before_qty and after_qty (nullable: false) cannot be filled, so the model yields no row rather than a row with null quantities. hole.deletions reserves row existence for such a pair as undecided ('whether a pair whose only reports are D-flagged has a holding_change row at all is undecided here too -- row existence, not only the values within an existing row'). This SQL does not resolve that; it states the question so the current no-row behavior is recognized as one behavior consistent with the hole, not an answer to it. Should a D-only pair (1) never appear, as today, (2) appear with quantities held at some other stated value, or (3) be treated as an error the pipeline should fail on?",
    "Is sources-v1.json's trade_code_meanings.cdc_flag a closed vocabulary ({I, U, D}, plus null for a historical Batch1 row), or could a raw.holding_history report carry some other flag value? The candidate set feeding latest_change (holding_change.sql's latest_report CTE and audits/inv.holding_quantity_updates_in_place.sql's eligible CTE) enumerates the anchored codes directly (cdc_flag IS NULL OR cdc_flag IN ('I', 'U')), so an out-of-vocabulary flag is today simply dropped from that set rather than treated as a candidate report. inv.eligible_holding_report_persisted's expected set instead abstains only on D (BOOL_AND(cdc_flag IS DISTINCT FROM 'D')), per the invariant's own wording; its parallel_assumption separately describes the candidate set as 'every raw.holding_history report for the pair is either I, U, or a historical row.' Which reading defines the latest_change candidate set: every non-D report (hole.deletions' framing), or every I, U, or historical report (the invariant's parallel_assumption)? An out-of-vocabulary-flag report is dropped by this projection today and surfaces only through inv.eligible_holding_report_persisted firing on the resulting zero-row pair; this SQL does not resolve which reading is correct, only that the two differ on this case."
  ],
